## Content Insights

Through this week's practical activity, I found that WordPress is more user-friendly than Joomla, especially for beginners. Its dashboard is intuitive, and creating pages or changing themes is relatively straightforward. However, I also realised that understanding which features are necessary for a project is important, as WordPress provides many options that can be overwhelming at first.

Building the website helped me understand the role of Content Management Systems (CMS) in modern web development. I learned that developing a website is not only about technical implementation but also about organising information effectively and creating a positive user experience through clear navigation and layout design.

In addition, reusing content from my previous Joomla project demonstrated the importance of planning and content management. Good preparation can significantly improve efficiency and reduce duplicated work during development.

---

## Employability / Learning Insights

The group formation activity provided valuable insights into teamwork and professional communication. During the one-minute interviews with classmates, I asked questions about their working styles, availability, technical skills, and expectations for group work.

This experience highlighted that effective team members require more than technical competence. Qualities such as reliability, responsibility, communication skills, and commitment to deadlines are equally important. Selecting group members with compatible goals and expectations can contribute significantly to the success of a project.

From a learning perspective, I found that a "learn by doing" approach was particularly effective. Encountering real problems while building the WordPress site encouraged me to search for solutions independently and apply new knowledge immediately. This process improved both my confidence and problem-solving abilities.

Overall, this week's activities enhanced my technical skills in WordPress while also strengthening my understanding of teamwork, communication, and professional collaboration.
